Package: lcos-base
Version: 0.9.1-3
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: 144
Maintainer: LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>
Homepage: https://lunduke.com
Depends: lcos-archive-keyring (>= 0.7), lcos-branding (>= 0.9-1)
Recommends: eject, cifs-utils, keyutils
Replaces: base-files
Description: LCOS 0.9.1 identity, GRUB drop-in, X/boot-order system config
 os-release / issue for LCOS 0.9.1 (excalibur), lcos-write-os-release,
 and /etc/default/grub.d/lcos.cfg (BACKGROUND lcos-splash-1024x768.png,
 GFXMODE=1024x768, GFXPAYLOAD keep, CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT quiet splash
 loglevel=2).
 .
 AMD GPUs (0.9.1-2, #115/#118): /etc/init.d/lcos-amdgpu-ddx (rcS, after
 udev) runs /usr/lib/lcos/lcos-amdgpu-ddx at every boot. It copies the 0.9
 modesetting+glamor OutputClass snippets from /usr/share/lcos/xorg into
 /usr/share/X11/xorg.conf.d only when every GPU bound to the amdgpu kernel
 driver is Vega/GFX9 or newer (not in the frozen pre-Vega PCI ID list from
 the kernel's amdgpu pciidlist), and removes them otherwise, so SI, CIK,
 VI and Polaris parts get the amdgpu DDX again as in 0.8. Override with
 lcos.amdgpu=modesetting|amdgpu on the kernel command line or in
 /etc/lcos/amdgpu-ddx.
 .
 insserv overrides so LightDM starts after elogind/seatd
 and /etc/init.d/plymouth no longer quits Plymouth at boot (LightDM is the
 single Plymouth quitter; the shutdown splash is kept).
 .
 Depends on the overlay keyring and branding artwork.
 0.9.1: recommends eject (#104) and cifs-utils + keyutils (#111). From
 0.9.1-3 they are Recommends, not Depends, so the Updates tool's plain
 apt-get upgrade moves 0.8 systems without holding lcos-base back.
 Postinst re-applies identity on configure so apt upgrades overwrite
 stale 0.4 conffile text kept by noninteractive Updates.
